-- CODEX INSURANCE LIMITED policy — encoding of the contract, rules only.
--
-- All dates/times other than the claimant's age are represented as NUMBER offsets
-- in months relative to the policy's effective date (per the task instructions: no
-- elapsed-time-between-two-dates calculation is ever required, so the DATE type is
-- not needed anywhere in this file).
--
-- Section 1.1(1) "this agreement is signed" and 1.1(2) "the applicable premium ...
-- has been paid" are ASSUMED throughout (per task instructions) and are therefore
-- not modelled as checkable facts on the Claim record.

§ `Definitions`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS A NUMBER
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS A NUMBER
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS A NUMBER
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS A BOOLEAN

§ `1. Policy in effect and conditions`

§§ `1.3 — wellness-visit confirmation deadline`

-- "... you will supply us with written confirmation ... of a wellness visit for
-- yourself with a qualified medical provider occurring no later than the 6th month
-- anniversary of the effective date of this policy" — two separate temporal limbs:
-- the visit itself must occur by month 6, and confirmation of it must be supplied
-- by month 7.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the wellness visit occurred in time` claim MEANS
    claim's `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred` AT MOST 6

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the confirmation of the wellness visit was supplied in time` claim MEANS
    claim's `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` AT MOST 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim MEANS
        `the wellness visit occurred in time` claim
    AND `the confirmation of the wellness visit was supplied in time` claim

-- 1.1(3): "is still pending" — the 7-month deadline for supplying confirmation has
-- not yet arrived, measured as of the hospitalization (the moment at which "policy
-- in effect" is being asked). While pending, the claimant gets the benefit of the
-- doubt: the deadline has not yet been missed.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 still pending` claim MEANS
    claim's `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred` AT MOST 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 pending or satisfied` claim MEANS
        `condition 1.3 still pending` claim
    OR  `condition 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim

§§ `1.2 — cancelation`

-- Read literally and in isolation, "cancelation ... if the condition set out in
-- Section 1.3 has not been satisfied in a timely fashion" would cancel the policy
-- from day one, before the 7-month deadline even arrives — which would make 1.1(3)'s
-- express "is still pending" carve-out meaningless. Harmonized here so that
-- cancelation on this ground requires the deadline to have actually passed (i.e.
-- NOT still pending) without a timely satisfaction; see NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled for a late wellness-visit confirmation` claim MEANS
    NOT `condition 1.3 pending or satisfied` claim

-- 3.6: the policy term is one year from the effective date; 1.2: the policy is
-- automatically canceled on the last day of that term.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled at the end of the policy term` claim MEANS
    claim's `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred` GREATER THAN 12

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` claim MEANS
        claim's `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`
    OR  `policy canceled for a late wellness-visit confirmation` claim
    OR  `policy canceled at the end of the policy term` claim

§§ `1.1 — policy in effect`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim MEANS
        `condition 1.3 pending or satisfied` claim          -- 1.1(3)
    AND NOT `policy canceled` claim                          -- 1.1(4)

-- "... hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury on which the claim for
-- such benefit is premised."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim MEANS
        claim's `for sickness`
    OR  claim's `for accidental injury`

§ `2. General exclusions`

-- "Your policy will not apply to, and no benefit will be paid with respect to, any
-- event causing sickness or accidental injury arising directly or indirectly out
-- of: 1. Skydiving; or 2. Service in the military; or 3. Service as a fire
-- fighter; or 4. Service in the police; or 5. [age >= 80]."
--
-- Each of the four activity exclusions is modelled as a CAUSAL fact — "arose
-- directly or indirectly out of" the activity — not as a mere status of the
-- claimant at the time of hospitalization. Merely holding a job (soldier,
-- firefighter, police officer) at the time of an unrelated injury does not, on
-- this reading, trigger the exclusion; the injury must actually arise from that
-- service. See NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`general exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        "(1) skydiving"              ... claim's `due to skydiving`
    ..  "(2) military service"       ... claim's `due to service in the military`
    ..  "(3) fire fighter service"   ... claim's `due to service as a fire fighter`
    ..  "(4) police service"         ... claim's `due to service in the police`
    OR  "(5) age at least 80"        ... claim's `age at the time of hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

-- 3. General conditions — none of these add a further gate on substantive coverage,
-- so (unlike Parts 1 and 2 above) this part carries no `§` section of its own; each
-- clause is noted here for completeness/auditability only.
--
-- 3.1 "Your Policy insures You twenty-four (24) hours a day anywhere in the world."
--     No territorial or time-of-day exclusion exists anywhere in this contract, so
--     there is nothing to gate.
-- 3.2 Arbitration — a claims-recovery / dispute-resolution precondition (referral to
--     arbitration, the 60-day wait after proof of claim, extinguishment for failing
--     to arbitrate within 3 months of an impasse), not a condition of substantive
--     coverage. None of the benchmark questions posit a dispute, so this is not
--     wired into `covered` below.
-- 3.3-3.5 Governing law, currency, and premium timing are boilerplate with no
--     bearing on whether a given hospitalization is covered. 3.5's lump-sum timing
--     is covered by the task's standing assumption that the premium has already
--     been paid on time.
-- 3.6 Policy term: one year from the effective date. See
--     `policy canceled at the end of the policy term` above, which implements the
--     automatic cancelation this section and 1.2 together describe.

§ `Top-level decision`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered` claim MEANS
        `policy in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim
    AND `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim
    AND NOT `general exclusion applies` claim
